IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ssaa-overpayment-dates`

-- Social Security (Administration) Act 1999 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- what a person who has been paid a social security
-- payment meets when the Department says they were overpaid: decisions made by computer (ss 6A, 83, 236); notice of a
-- decision (s 237); the Secretary's information-gathering notices and what follows from ignoring them (Part 5 Division 1:
-- ss 191A-198); the offences of Part 6 (ss 211-219, 223, 224, 233) and the repayment order a court may add; and the ART
-- provisions that bear on a contested overpayment (ss 176, 181, 182, 183).
--
-- SEAT: the person who claims, receives or has received a social security payment and is told that they were overpaid, is
-- asked to explain their income, or is accused of an offence. "Is a decision a computer made about me a real decision? When
-- was I given notice? Must I answer this letter, and by when? What if I don't? Can what I say be used against me? What is
-- the most a court can do to me? What happens to my appeal if the debt case settles?" What the Secretary, the ART or a court
-- decides is asked as a fact ("if the Secretary considers ...", "if the court accepts ...").
--
-- A LAYER BESIDE baseline-2026-10 (../baseline-2026-10/), which stays untouched: it answers the claim, the start day,
-- reporting duties (ss 66A-74), mutual obligations, the date of effect of an adverse decision (s 118) and review (ss 109,
-- 126-131, 142-147). Nothing here restates it. Whether a debt exists, and its amount, recovery, write-off and waiver, are
-- the Social Security Act 1991's (Chapter 5, Part 5.2), not this Act's, and are not encoded here. The stable l4 cannot
-- IMPORT across encoding folders; NOTES.md names the links.
--
-- Every exported question takes plain facts. No question takes a DEONTIC or an EVENT. The two duties with deadlines the
-- person meets -- comply with a s 196 notice within its period (s 197(1)), and tell the Department a new address within 14
-- days (s 193(b)) -- are regulative rules run inside the questions by EVALTRACE.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 163, compilation date 5 December 2025, includes amendments up to Act No. 73, 2025 (register id
-- C2026C00010, in 2 volumes), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00580.txt.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the seat of the person paid, with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Social Security (Administration) Act 1999 -- overpayment, information notices and offences: the person's questions`

§§ `ss 6A, 236 -- a decision made by a computer`

-- s 236(1): "A decision of an officer under the social security law must be in writing." (2): "A decision under the social
-- security law is taken to be in writing if it is made, or recorded, by means of a computer." s 6A(1): the Secretary "may
-- arrange for the use ... of computer programs for any purposes for which the Secretary or any other officer may make
-- decisions"; (2): "A decision made by the operation of a computer program under an arrangement made under subsection (1)
-- is taken to be a decision made by the Secretary."
DECLARE `How the decision was made` IS ONE OF
    `by an officer, on paper or recorded on a computer`
    `by the operation of a computer program the Secretary arranged to use (s 6A)`
    `by an officer, only spoken, with no written or computer record`

DECLARE `What the decision is in law` IS ONE OF
    `a decision in writing (s 236) of the officer who made it`
    `a decision in writing (s 236(2)) taken to be made by the Secretary (s 6A(2))`
    `not a decision in writing, as s 236(1) requires a decision of an officer to be`

@export A decision about my payment or debt was made by a computer, or only told to me over the phone. Does it count as a decision in writing, and whose decision is it (ss 6A, 236)?
GIVEN `how it was made` IS A `How the decision was made` @desc How the decision was made: by an officer on paper or recorded on a computer, by a computer program the Secretary arranged to use, or by an officer only spoken with no written or computer record
GIVETH A `What the decision is in law`
`What is the decision about me in law` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how it was made`
    WHEN `by an officer, on paper or recorded on a computer` THEN `a decision in writing (s 236) of the officer who made it`
    WHEN `by the operation of a computer program the Secretary arranged to use (s 6A)` THEN `a decision in writing (s 236(2)) taken to be made by the Secretary (s 6A(2))`
    WHEN `by an officer, only spoken, with no written or computer record` THEN `not a decision in writing, as s 236(1) requires a decision of an officer to be`

-- s 83(1): "If: (a) payment of a social security payment is based upon data in a computer; and (b) the rate of the payment is
-- increased or reduced, or the payment is cancelled or suspended, because of the operation of a computer program used under
-- the control of the Secretary; and (c) the program causes the change for a reason for which the Secretary could make the
-- change by determination; the change is taken to have been made by the Secretary by determination for that reason." (2):
-- the determination "is taken to have been made on the day on which the computer program caused the change to be made".
-- NOTHING: s 83 does not deem a determination on these facts (an "if" that fails; what the change is then is not this
-- section's to say).
@export A computer cut, cancelled or suspended my payment. Is that taken to be the Secretary's determination, and made on what day (s 83)?
GIVEN `my payment is based on data in a computer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your payment is worked out from data held in a computer
      `a computer program the Secretary controls made the change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the rate went up or down, or the payment was cancelled or suspended, because of a computer program used under the Secretary's control
      `the Secretary could have made the change for that reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the reason the program made the change is one for which the Secretary could make the change by determination
      `the day the program made the change` IS A DATE @desc The day the computer program caused the change
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`On what day is the computer's change taken to be a determination` MEANS
    IF `my payment is based on data in a computer` AND `a computer program the Secretary controls made the change` AND `the Secretary could have made the change for that reason`
    THEN JUST `the day the program made the change`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 237 -- when notice of a decision is taken to have been given to me`

-- s 237(1): notice of a decision "(a) delivered to a person personally; or (b) left at the address of the place of residence
-- or business of the person last known to the Secretary; or (c) sent by prepaid post to the postal address of the person
-- last known to the Secretary" is "taken ... to have been given to the person". (2)-(3): posted notice "is taken to have been
-- given to the person at the time at which the notice would be delivered in the ordinary course of the post unless the
-- contrary is proved". (4): "This section only applies to notices of decisions" (other notices: Acts Interpretation Act
-- 1901 ss 28A, 29, not encoded). s 5 lets a written notice be given "in a manner approved by the Secretary" (an online
-- account, for example); s 237 does not say when such a notice is given, so that answers NOTHING.
-- The day of notice matters for review: within 13 weeks of it a win goes back to the start (s 109; baseline-2026-10).
DECLARE `How the notice reached me` IS ONE OF
    `handed to me personally`
    `left at my last home or business address the Secretary knew`
    `posted, prepaid, to my last postal address the Secretary knew`
    `another way, such as my online account`
    `it is not a notice of a decision`

@export On what day is notice of a Centrelink decision taken to have been given to me (s 237)?
GIVEN `how` IS A `How the notice reached me` @desc How the notice reached you: handed to you, left at your last known home or business address, posted to your last known postal address, another way (such as your online account), or it is not a notice of a decision
      `the day it was handed to me or left` IS A DATE @desc The day it was handed to you or left at the address (ignored if posted)
      `the day it would arrive in the ordinary course of post` IS A DATE @desc For a posted notice, the day it would be delivered in the ordinary course of post
      `I can prove it arrived on another day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a posted notice, whether you can prove it was in fact delivered on a different day
      `the day it actually arrived` IS A DATE @desc For a posted notice, the day it was in fact delivered (used only if you can prove it)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`On what day was notice of the decision given to me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how`
    WHEN `handed to me personally` THEN JUST `the day it was handed to me or left`
    WHEN `left at my last home or business address the Secretary knew` THEN JUST `the day it was handed to me or left`
    WHEN `posted, prepaid, to my last postal address the Secretary knew` THEN
        IF `I can prove it arrived on another day`
        THEN JUST `the day it actually arrived`
        ELSE JUST `the day it would arrive in the ordinary course of post`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `ss 191A-194, 198(2) -- can the Department make me give information or documents`

-- (Situation: I have been sent, or expect, a letter asking for payslips, bank statements or other information.)
-- s 191A: "The Secretary can only require a person to: (a) give information; or (b) produce a document; under this Division if
-- the Secretary reasonably believes that the person will be able to give the information or produce the document."
-- s 192: the Secretary "may require a person to give information, or produce a document ... if the Secretary considers that
-- the information or document may be relevant to" qualification, payability, rate, concession cards, financial supplement,
-- and others, "(k) an inquiry or investigation into a matter" in those paragraphs.
-- s 193: of "a person who owes a debt to the Commonwealth under or as a result of the social security law": "(a) ...
-- information ... [or] a document that is relevant to the person's financial situation; and (b) if the person's address
-- changes--to inform the Department of the new address within 14 days after the change".
-- s 194: of any person, information that "(a) would help the Department locate another person (the debtor) who owes a debt
-- ... or (b) is relevant to the debtor's financial situation", if the Secretary considers so.
-- s 198(2): "This Division does not require a person to give information or produce a document to the extent that in doing
-- so the person would contravene a law of the Commonwealth (other than a law of a Territory)."
-- Answers: JUST FALSE where s 198(2) or s 191A says no, or where the "if" of s 192 or s 194 fails; NOTHING where the purpose is
-- outside ss 192-194 (other powers, such as ss 63 and 67-70, are not this Division's) or where I owe no debt and the purpose
-- is s 193 (a scope limit without "only"; s 192 may still reach me).
DECLARE `What the information is about` IS ONE OF
    `my qualification for, or the payability or rate of, a payment, card or financial supplement, or an inquiry into it (s 192)`
    `my own financial situation, as a person who owes a debt under the social security law (s 193)`
    `where another person who owes a debt is, or that person's financial situation (s 194)`
    `something else`

@export Can Services Australia make me give this information or produce this document (ss 191A, 192, 193, 194, 198(2))?
GIVEN `what it is about` IS A `What the information is about` @desc What the information or document is about: your qualification, payment or rate (or an inquiry into it); your own finances as someone who owes a social security debt; finding, or the finances of, someone else who owes such a debt; or something else
      `the Secretary considers it may be relevant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary considers the information may be relevant to that matter (for a debt you owe yourself, whether it is relevant to your financial situation)
      `I owe a debt under the social security law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you owe a debt to the Commonwealth under or as a result of the social security law
      `the Secretary reasonably believes I can give it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary reasonably believes you are able to give the information or produce the document
      `giving it would break a Commonwealth law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether giving it would make you contravene a law of the Commonwealth (not a Territory law)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I be required to give it` MEANS
    IF `giving it would break a Commonwealth law` OR (NOT `the Secretary reasonably believes I can give it`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE `by what it is about`
    WHERE
        `by what it is about` MEANS
            CONSIDER `what it is about`
            WHEN `my qualification for, or the payability or rate of, a payment, card or financial supplement, or an inquiry into it (s 192)` THEN JUST `the Secretary considers it may be relevant`
            WHEN `my own financial situation, as a person who owes a debt under the social security law (s 193)` THEN
                IF `I owe a debt under the social security law` THEN JUST `the Secretary considers it may be relevant` ELSE NOTHING
            WHEN `where another person who owes a debt is, or that person's financial situation (s 194)` THEN JUST `the Secretary considers it may be relevant`
            OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 196 -- what the notice must say, and the shortest time it may give me`

-- s 196(1): "A requirement under this Division must be made by written notice given to the person". (2)(b): the notice "must
-- specify: (ia) a description of the information or document ...; (i) how the person is to give the information or produce
-- the document ...; (ii) the period within which the person is to give the information or produce the document ...; (iii) the
-- officer (if any) to whom the information is to be given ...; and (iv) that the notice is given under this section". (3):
-- "the period must not end earlier than 14 days after the notice is given, unless the Secretary is satisfied that it is
-- reasonable in the circumstances ... to specify a shorter period". (4)-(6): a notice requiring me to appear before an officer
-- must specify "(a) a time and place at which the person is to appear; and (b) that the person may be accompanied by a
-- lawyer", and "the time must be at least 14 days after the notice is given", with the same exception.
-- "14 days after" day G: the period excludes G (Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 36(1)), so it may end no earlier than G + 14.
@export What is the earliest day a notice requiring information may set for me to answer it, or to appear before an officer (s 196(3), (6))? (A shorter time is allowed only if the Secretary is satisfied it is reasonable.)
GIVEN `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc The day the notice was given to you
GIVETH A DATE
`The earliest day the notice may set` `the day the notice was given` MEANS `n days after` `the day the notice was given` 14

@export Does the notice requiring me to give information or documents meet the requirements of s 196?
GIVEN `it is a written notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the requirement was made by a written notice given to you
      `it describes the information or documents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice describes the information or documents required (a class is enough)
      `it says how to give them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice says how you are to give the information or produce the documents
      `it says the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice states the period within which you must give them
      `it names the officer if there is one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice names the officer you must give them to, if they are to go to a particular officer (answer yes if no particular officer is involved)
      `it says it is given under s 196` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice says that it is given under section 196 of the Social Security (Administration) Act 1999
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc The day the notice was given to you
      `the last day it gives me` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the period the notice gives you
      `it requires me to appear before an officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice requires you to appear before an officer to answer questions
      `it gives a time and place and says I may bring a lawyer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a notice to appear, whether it states a time and place and that you may be accompanied by a lawyer
      `the day I must appear` IS A DATE @desc For a notice to appear, the day you must appear
      `the Secretary was satisfied a shorter time was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary was satisfied that a shorter period, or an earlier time to appear, was reasonable in the circumstances
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the notice meet s 196` IF
        `it is a written notice`
    AND `it describes the information or documents`
    AND `it says how to give them`
    AND `it says the period`
    AND `it names the officer if there is one`
    AND `it says it is given under s 196`
    AND (`days between` `the earliest day` `the last day it gives me` AT LEAST 0 OR `the Secretary was satisfied a shorter time was reasonable`)
    AND (    (NOT `it requires me to appear before an officer`)
         OR (    `it gives a time and place and says I may bring a lawyer`
             AND (`days between` `the earliest day` `the day I must appear` AT LEAST 0 OR `the Secretary was satisfied a shorter time was reasonable`)))
    WHERE
        `the earliest day` MEANS `The earliest day the notice may set` `the day the notice was given`

§§ `ss 197, 197A, 198(2) -- what happens if I do not comply`

DECLARE `Person required` IS ONE OF `the person required`
DECLARE `Information step` IS ONE OF
    `give the information or produce the document`
    `inform the Department of my new address`

-- s 197(1): "A person must not refuse or fail to comply with a requirement under this Division to give information or produce
-- a document. Penalty: Imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months." Written as the person's duty to comply within the
-- period the notice gives, with the breach naming the offence.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Person required` `Information step`
`s 197(1) -- comply within the period the notice gives` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the person required`
    MUST `give the information or produce the document`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person required` BECAUSE "the information was not given, or the document not produced, within the period the s 196 notice gives: an offence against s 197(1), unless s 197(2), s 197(3) or s 198(2) applies; imprisonment for up to 12 months"

-- s 193(b): a person who owes a debt may be required, "if the person's address changes--to inform the Department of the new
-- address within 14 days after the change". The day of the change is day 0.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Person required` `Information step`
`s 193(b) -- tell the Department my new address within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY `the person required`
    MUST `inform the Department of my new address`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person required` BECAUSE "the new address was not given to the Department within 14 days after the change, as a s 193(b) requirement asks: a failure to comply with a requirement under Part 5 Division 1 (s 197(1), a reading; see NOTES.md)"

-- Runs a rule over one step taken on one day. On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH,
-- so FULFILLED means in time and anything else late. Not exported; it takes no DEONTIC from outside.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Person required` `Information step`, `the step` IS AN `Information step`, `the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `taking the step on this day keeps the rule` `the rule` `the step` `the day` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day`), (EVENT `the person required` `the step` `the day`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 197(2): "Subsection (1) applies only to the extent to which the person is capable of complying with the requirement." (3):
-- "Subsection (1) does not apply if the person has a reasonable excuse." s 197A(1): "A person is not excused from giving
-- information, or producing a document, under this Division on the ground that the information, or production of the
-- document, might tend to incriminate the person or expose the person to a penalty." s 198(2) (above).
-- A requirement not made by a notice that meets s 196 is read as no requirement under the Division, so s 197 does not reach
-- it (fork F1 in NOTES.md: the other reading is that a defect short of s 196(1) leaves the requirement standing).
DECLARE `Why I did not comply` IS ONE OF
    `no particular reason`
    `it might incriminate me or expose me to a penalty`
    `another reason that may be a reasonable excuse`
    `complying would break a Commonwealth law`

DECLARE `Do I commit the s 197 offence` IS ONE OF
    `no offence: you complied within the period the notice gives`
    `not yet: the period the notice gives has not ended; comply by its last day`
    `s 197 does not apply: the requirement was not made by a notice that meets s 196`
    `no offence: this Division does not require you to break a Commonwealth law (s 198(2))`
    `no offence to the extent you were not capable of complying (s 197(2))`
    `no offence if you have a reasonable excuse (s 197(3)); whether the excuse is reasonable is for the court`
    `an offence against s 197(1), imprisonment for up to 12 months: fear of self-incrimination or a penalty is no excuse (s 197A(1)), though what you give cannot be used against you in most criminal proceedings (s 197A(2))`
    `an offence against s 197(1): imprisonment for up to 12 months`

@export I received a notice requiring me to give information or produce documents. Do I commit an offence if I do not comply, or comply late (ss 197, 197A, 198(2))?
GIVEN `the notice meets s 196` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice met the requirements of s 196 (a written notice saying what is required, how, by when, and that it is given under s 196)
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc The day the notice was given to you
      `the last day it gives me` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the period the notice gives you
      `I have complied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the information or produced the documents
      `the day I complied` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave the information or produced the documents (ignored if you have not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
      `I was capable of complying` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were able to give the information or produce the documents
      `why not` IS A `Why I did not comply` @desc Why you did not comply in time: no particular reason; it might incriminate you or expose you to a penalty; another reason that may be a reasonable excuse; or complying would break a Commonwealth law
GIVETH A `Do I commit the s 197 offence`
`Do I commit an offence by not complying` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the notice meets s 196`)
            THEN `s 197 does not apply: the requirement was not made by a notice that meets s 196`
        IF `I have complied` AND `complied in time`
            THEN `no offence: you complied within the period the notice gives`
        IF (NOT `I have complied`) AND `days between` `today` `the last day it gives me` AT LEAST 0
            THEN `not yet: the period the notice gives has not ended; comply by its last day`
        IF `why not` EQUALS `complying would break a Commonwealth law`
            THEN `no offence: this Division does not require you to break a Commonwealth law (s 198(2))`
        IF (NOT `I was capable of complying`)
            THEN `no offence to the extent you were not capable of complying (s 197(2))`
        IF `why not` EQUALS `another reason that may be a reasonable excuse`
            THEN `no offence if you have a reasonable excuse (s 197(3)); whether the excuse is reasonable is for the court`
        IF `why not` EQUALS `it might incriminate me or expose me to a penalty`
            THEN `an offence against s 197(1), imprisonment for up to 12 months: fear of self-incrimination or a penalty is no excuse (s 197A(1)), though what you give cannot be used against you in most criminal proceedings (s 197A(2))`
        OTHERWISE `an offence against s 197(1): imprisonment for up to 12 months`
    WHERE
        `the days allowed` MEANS `days between` `the day the notice was given` `the last day it gives me`
        `complied in time` MEANS `taking the step on this day keeps the rule` (`s 197(1) -- comply within the period the notice gives` `the days allowed`) `give the information or produce the document` (`days between` `the day the notice was given` `the day I complied`)

-- s 197A(2): "in the case of an individual: (a) the information given or document produced; and (b) giving the information or
-- producing the document; and (c) any information, document or thing obtained as a direct or indirect consequence ...; are not
-- admissible in evidence against the individual in any criminal proceedings, other than: (d) proceedings for an offence
-- against subsection 197(1); or (e) ... section 137.1 or 137.2 of the Criminal Code that relates to this Division; or (f) ...
-- Division 145 of the Criminal Code; or (g) ... section 217 that relates: (i) to this Division; and (ii) to a contravention of
-- subsection 212(1), 213(1), 214(1), 214(2) or 216(3)." s 197B: "Subject to subsection 197A(2), nothing in this Division
-- prevents information given ... from being used in: (a) an inquiry or investigation into a matter; or (b) criminal
-- proceedings." Civil proceedings (debt recovery among them) are not mentioned by either: NOTHING.
DECLARE `Where it would be used` IS ONE OF
    `criminal proceedings for not complying with the requirement (s 197(1))`
    `criminal proceedings for false or misleading information or documents (Criminal Code s 137.1 or 137.2) relating to the requirement`
    `criminal proceedings for an offence in Criminal Code Division 145 (using forged documents and related offences)`
    `criminal proceedings under s 217 for a false statement or document (s 212(1), 213(1), 214(1), 214(2) or 216(3)) relating to the requirement`
    `other criminal proceedings against me`
    `an inquiry or investigation`
    `civil proceedings, such as recovering a debt`

@export Can what I give in answer to an information notice (or anything found because of it) be used against me (ss 197A(2), 197B)?
GIVEN `where` IS A `Where it would be used` @desc Where it would be used: a prosecution for not complying; a prosecution for false or misleading information or documents (Criminal Code s 137.1 or 137.2); a Criminal Code Division 145 prosecution; a s 217 prosecution for a false statement or document; other criminal proceedings; an inquiry or investigation; or civil proceedings such as debt recovery
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can what I give be used against me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `where`
    WHEN `other criminal proceedings against me` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `civil proceedings, such as recovering a debt` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 193(b), run as a rule (above).
DECLARE `Did I give my new address in time` IS ONE OF
    `s 193(b) does not apply: no notice required you to tell the Department of a change of address`
    `in time: you told the Department within 14 days after the change`
    `still in time: tell the Department within 14 days after the change`
    `late: you did not tell the Department within 14 days after the change, as the requirement asks`

@export I owe a social security debt and was required to tell the Department if my address changes. Did I tell them in time (s 193(b))?
GIVEN `a notice required me to tell the Department of a new address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a notice under s 193 required you, as a person who owes a social security debt, to tell the Department if your address changes
      `the day my address changed` IS A DATE @desc The day your address changed
      `I have told the Department` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have told the Department your new address
      `the day I told them` IS A DATE @desc The day you told the Department (ignored if you have not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Did I give my new address in time`
`Did I tell the Department my new address in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `a notice required me to tell the Department of a new address`)
            THEN `s 193(b) does not apply: no notice required you to tell the Department of a change of address`
        IF `I have told the Department` AND `told in time`
            THEN `in time: you told the Department within 14 days after the change`
        IF (NOT `I have told the Department`) AND `days between` `the day my address changed` `today` AT MOST 14
            THEN `still in time: tell the Department within 14 days after the change`
        OTHERWISE `late: you did not tell the Department within 14 days after the change, as the requirement asks`
    WHERE
        `told in time` MEANS `taking the step on this day keeps the rule` `s 193(b) -- tell the Department my new address within 14 days` `inform the Department of my new address` (`days between` `the day my address changed` `the day I told them`)

§§ `s 195 -- information about me that others are made to give`

-- (Situation: the Department asks an employer, bank, educational institution or other body for information about a class of
-- people that includes me, to detect payments that should not have been made or to verify claims.)
-- s 195(2): the information that may be required "about each person in the class of persons is all or any of the following
-- information (but no other information)": a closed list, so information outside it answers JUST FALSE.
-- s 195(4): "Within 13 weeks after information is given ..., the Secretary must decide which (if any) of the information is,
-- or is likely to be, relevant". (5): information decided irrelevant within that time: "any record of the irrelevant
-- information is destroyed". (6): "If the Secretary has not made a decision ... at the end of the 13 week period, the Secretary
-- must ensure that any record of all or any part of the information is destroyed." 13 weeks = 91 days.
DECLARE `What they want to know about me` IS ONE OF
    `my name, address, sex, marital status, date of birth or death, or my entries to and departures from Australia (s 195(2)(a)-(g))`
    `payments the body gave me in the 52 weeks before the notice, and the account they were paid into (s 195(2)(h))`
    `my real property: owner, address, title details (s 195(2)(ha))`
    `my course of study: the items s 195(2)(i) lists`
    `the start and end dates of my employment with the body asked (s 195(2)(j))`
    `my income stream: the items s 195(2)(ja) lists`
    `my child's school enrolment or attendance, or my compliance with a schooling compliance notice (s 195(2)(k), (l))`
    `anything else, such as my hours worked or my bank balance`

@export Can the Department make an employer, bank or other body give it this information about me under s 195?
GIVEN `what` IS A `What they want to know about me` @desc What the body is asked to give about you, from the list in s 195(2), or anything else (such as your hours worked or your bank balance)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a body be made to give this about me under s 195` IF
    CONSIDER `what`
    WHEN `anything else, such as my hours worked or my bank balance` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

@export By what day must the Secretary decide whether information a body gave about me under s 195 is relevant (s 195(4))?
GIVEN `the day the information was given` IS A DATE @desc The day the body gave the information to the Department
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must the Secretary decide on the s 195 information` `the day the information was given` MEANS `n days after` `the day the information was given` 91

@export Must the record of information a body gave about me under s 195 be destroyed (s 195(5), (6))?
GIVEN `the day the information was given` IS A DATE @desc The day the body gave the information to the Department
      `the Secretary decided within 13 weeks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary decided, within 13 weeks after it was given, which of the information is or is likely to be relevant
      `the Secretary decided it was relevant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the Secretary decided in time, whether the information about you was decided to be relevant
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the s 195 record about me be destroyed` IF
    IF `the Secretary decided within 13 weeks`
    THEN (NOT `the Secretary decided it was relevant`)
    ELSE `days between` `the day the information was given` `today` GREATER THAN 91

§§ `ss 211-216 -- the offences of Part 6`

-- (Situation: I am told I may be prosecuted over a claim, a statement or a payment.) s 211: the Part extends to everyone who
-- has claimed, or is receiving or has received, a payment, and to acts outside Australia.
-- ss 212(1), 213(1), 214(1), (2), 216(1), (3): "A person contravenes this subsection if: ..." -- defined by their elements, so
-- an element that fails answers JUST FALSE. s 215(1): "A person must not obtain ... knowing that the payment is (c) not payable
-- at all; or (d) only payable in part" -- a prohibition limited in its own words: without that knowledge it answers NOTHING.
-- "Reckless" is the Criminal Code's (s 5.4, borrowed): aware of a substantial risk and unjustifiably taking it; knowledge or
-- intention also satisfies it (s 5.4(4)). Asked as a fact.
DECLARE `What I did` IS ONE OF
    `made a statement in connection with, or in support of, my or another person's claim, or a hardship request under 1991 Act s 1129 or 1131 (s 212)`
    `made a statement (s 213)`
    `made a statement to an officer or Services Australia (s 214(1))`
    `presented a document to an officer or Services Australia (s 214(2))`
    `obtained a payment or instalment (s 215)`
    `obtained a payment or instalment by impersonation or a fraudulent device (s 216(1))`
    `obtained a payment or instalment as a result of a statement I made (s 216(3))`

@export Do the facts make out a contravention of Part 6 Division 2 (ss 212-216), an offence under s 217?
GIVEN `what I did` IS A `What I did` @desc What you did: made a statement about a claim or hardship request; made a statement that might deceive or affect a rate; made a statement to an officer or Services Australia; presented a document to them; obtained a payment; obtained a payment by impersonation or a fraudulent device; or obtained a payment as a result of a statement
      `it was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the statement or document was false or misleading (for s 214, in any particular)
      `I was reckless whether it was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were aware of a substantial risk that it was false or misleading and it was unjustifiable to take the risk (knowing it was false counts)
      `I was reckless whether it might deceive or affect a rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For s 213: whether you were reckless as to whether the statement might deceive an officer or Services Australia, or might affect the rate of a payment
      `I knew the payment was not payable or only partly payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For s 215: whether, when you obtained the payment, you knew it was not payable at all or only payable in part
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is it a contravention of Part 6 Division 2` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what I did`
    WHEN `made a statement (s 213)` THEN JUST (`false and reckless` AND `I was reckless whether it might deceive or affect a rate`)
    WHEN `obtained a payment or instalment (s 215)` THEN
        IF `I knew the payment was not payable or only partly payable` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `obtained a payment or instalment by impersonation or a fraudulent device (s 216(1))` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST `false and reckless`
    WHERE
        `false and reckless` MEANS `it was false or misleading` AND `I was reckless whether it was false or misleading`

§§ `ss 217-219, 223, 224, 233 -- the most a court can do`

-- s 217: "A person who contravenes a provision of Division 2 commits an offence punishable on conviction by imprisonment for a
-- term not exceeding 12 months." s 218(1)(b): the court may "order the person to pay the Commonwealth an amount equal to any
-- amount paid by way of social security payment because of the act, failure or omission that constituted the offence"; (2):
-- "a person is not to be imprisoned for failing to pay" it. s 219(2): a single penalty for several offences "must not exceed
-- the sum of the maximum penalties that could be imposed if a separate penalty were imposed for each offence". s 223: the
-- Secretary's certificate of the amount is "prima facie evidence". s 224: the court's certificate of the amount, filed, "is
-- enforceable ... as a final judgment". s 233: a person who "would not have been convicted if sections 231 and 232 had not
-- been in force" (convicted only through an employee's or agent's conduct or state of mind) "is not liable to be punished by
-- imprisonment". Fines instead of imprisonment (Crimes Act 1914 s 4B) are borrowed and not encoded.
DECLARE `The most a court can order` HAS
    `most months of imprisonment in all`         IS A NUMBER
    `most repayment the court can order`         IS A NUMBER
    `I can be imprisoned for not paying it`      IS A BOOLEAN

@export If I am convicted of social security offences under s 217, what is the most imprisonment, and the most repayment, a court can order (ss 217-219, 233)?
GIVEN `how many offences` IS A NUMBER @desc How many offences under s 217 you are convicted of
      `the amount paid because of the offences` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount, in dollars, paid to you by way of social security payment because of the acts, failures or omissions that were the offences
      `only through an employee's or agent's conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you would not have been convicted but for ss 231 and 232 (the conduct or state of mind of your employee or agent)
GIVETH A `The most a court can order`
`The most a court can order me` MEANS
    `The most a court can order` WITH
        `most months of imprisonment in all`    IS IF `only through an employee's or agent's conduct` THEN 0 ELSE 12 TIMES `how many offences`
        `most repayment the court can order`    IS `the amount paid because of the offences`
        `I can be imprisoned for not paying it` IS FALSE

§§ `ss 176, 181, 182, 183 -- at the ART`

-- (Situation: I have applied to the ART for review of a decision, such as one that I owe a debt.)
-- s 176(1): "a party to an ART review must bear any expenses incurred by the party in connection with the review." (2): the ART
-- "may determine that the Commonwealth is to pay the reasonable costs that are: (a) incurred by a party for travel and
-- accommodation ...; and (b) specified in the determination." (3)-(4): medical services the ART arranges, likewise.
@export How much of my own expenses of an ART review must I bear (s 176)?
GIVEN `my expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc Your expenses of the review, in dollars
      `travel and accommodation the ART determined the Commonwealth pays` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of your travel and accommodation costs, in dollars, that the ART has determined the Commonwealth is to pay (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of my expenses must I bear` MEANS
    IF `my expenses` AT LEAST `travel and accommodation the ART determined the Commonwealth pays`
    THEN `my expenses` MINUS `travel and accommodation the ART determined the Commonwealth pays`
    ELSE 0

-- s 181(1): "The Secretary may agree, in writing, with other parties to settle proceedings before the ART that relate to the
-- recovery of a debt." (2): "If proceedings are settled and the Secretary gives the ART a copy of the agreement ..., the
-- application for review ... is taken to have been dismissed." JUST FALSE when the "if" fails; NOTHING when the proceedings are
-- not about recovering a debt (the section's scope, without "only").
@export I settled my ART case about a social security debt. Is my application taken to be dismissed (s 181)?
GIVEN `the proceedings relate to recovering a debt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the ART proceedings relate to the recovery of a debt
      `we agreed in writing to settle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the Secretary (and any other party) agreed in writing to settle the proceedings
      `the Secretary gave the ART a copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary gave the ART a copy of the agreement
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my ART application taken to be dismissed` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the proceedings relate to recovering a debt`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`we agreed in writing to settle` AND `the Secretary gave the ART a copy`)

-- s 182(1): "If an officer varies or substitutes a decision after an application has been made to the ART ..., the application
-- is taken to be an application for review of the decision as varied or substituted." (2): "However, if the President of the
-- ART refers the application to the guidance and appeals panel ..., section 31 (decision cannot be altered outside Tribunal
-- process) of [the ART Act] applies to the decision after the referral is made."
DECLARE `What the ART reviews` IS ONE OF
    `the decision as it was when I applied`
    `the decision as varied or substituted (s 182(1))`
    `the decision as it was when referred: after referral to the guidance and appeals panel it cannot be altered outside the Tribunal's process (s 182(2), ART Act s 31)`

@export The decision was changed after I applied to the ART. Which decision does the ART now review (s 182)?
GIVEN `an officer changed the decision after I applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an officer varied the decision, or substituted another, after you applied to the ART
      `it had been referred to the guidance and appeals panel first` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the ART President had referred your application to the guidance and appeals panel before the change
GIVETH A `What the ART reviews`
`Which decision does the ART review` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `an officer changed the decision after I applied`)
            THEN `the decision as it was when I applied`
        IF `it had been referred to the guidance and appeals panel first`
            THEN `the decision as it was when referred: after referral to the guidance and appeals panel it cannot be altered outside the Tribunal's process (s 182(2), ART Act s 31)`
        OTHERWISE `the decision as varied or substituted (s 182(1))`

-- s 183: "If: (a) on ART review of a decision, the ART sets the decision aside; and (b) the Secretary or the ART ... is
-- satisfied that an event that did not occur would have occurred if the decision had not been made; the Secretary or the ART
-- may, if satisfied that it is reasonable to do so, treat the event as having occurred". Judgments, asked as facts; the
-- answer is the permission, not the outcome.
@export The ART set aside a decision against me. Can something that would have happened without that decision be treated as having happened (s 183)?
GIVEN `the ART set the decision aside` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on ART review, the ART set the decision aside
      `satisfied the event would have occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary or the ART is satisfied that the event (for example, a payment or a claim) would have occurred if the decision had not been made
      `satisfied it is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary or the ART is satisfied that it is reasonable to treat the event as having occurred
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the event be treated as having occurred` IF
        `the ART set the decision aside`
    AND `satisfied the event would have occurred`
    AND `satisfied it is reasonable`
